  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking issue** in `share-editing` compared with `main`:\n\n**[P1] View-only shares can edit unlocked documents — `src/guard.js:12`**\n\n`share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` is parsed as `share.mask & (WRITE === WRITE)`, which reduces to `share.mask & 1`. This checks the **READ** bit instead of WRITE.\n\nConfirmed:\n- `{ mask: READ, locked: false }` → editing **allowed**, despite being view-only.\n- `{ mask: WRITE, locked: false }` → editing **denied**, despite having WRITE.\n\nUse `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE)` or parenthesize `(share.mask & WRITE) === WRITE`. Add tests for a viewer being denied editing and a WRITE-only share being allowed; the existing editor test has both READ and WRITE, so it misses this bug.\n\nAll **6 existing tests pass**, but the additional permission checks reproduce the issue. No code or files changed.",
